#description: A definition holds the lineage, and a schema in the text declares a definition #T and refers to it. A schema's body includes its definitions, wherever the lineage is held; this is the case #265 broke.
#expect: ok
#spec: docs/invariants.md:116-118, docs/invariants.md:143-148
#at: lin.h
#known/fill-use: #270 bind rebuilds the lineage from its conjuncts without thema.Lineage; the use's conjunct, written in a definition, stays closed and has no schemas field (E0126).
#known/unify-use-text: #270 bind rebuilds the lineage from its conjuncts without thema.Lineage; the use's conjunct, written in a definition, stays closed and has no schemas field (E0126).
#known/unify-text-use: #270 bind rebuilds the lineage from its conjuncts without thema.Lineage; the use's conjunct, written in a definition, stays closed and has no schemas field (E0126).
#known/third-root: #270 bind rebuilds the lineage from its conjuncts without thema.Lineage; the use's conjunct, written in a definition, stays closed and has no schemas field (E0126).
-- in.cue --
import "github.com/sdboyer/thema"

#Op: h: thema.Lineage & {name: "h"}
lin: #Op
-- text.cue --
schemas: "0": "0": schema: {#T: string, a?: #T}
-- out/fill-text-named/bind --
verdict: ok
-- out/fill-text/bind --
verdict: ok
-- out/fill-use/bind --
verdict: E0126
E0126 the lineage is not an instance of thema.Lineage @ :1:1
-- out/third-root/bind --
verdict: E0126
E0126 the lineage is not an instance of thema.Lineage @ :1:1
-- out/together/bind --
verdict: ok
-- out/unify-text-use/bind --
verdict: E0126
E0126 the lineage is not an instance of thema.Lineage @ :1:1
-- out/unify-use-text/bind --
verdict: E0126
E0126 the lineage is not an instance of thema.Lineage @ no position
